#
# Conformance case: profiles/probabilistic-confidence-guard
# AC (#506): a logic:confidence annotation is NOT auto-interpreted as a probability
# (the guard test goes RED if violated). The diagnosis(patient, flu) fact is
# asserted in the EDB (input.nq) and carries confidence 0.9 (the
# `:- confidence(...)` directive in queries/diagnosis.logic). Under
# logic:ProbabilisticProfile with a declared model, the marginal of the asserted
# fact MUST be 1.0 — the confidence 0.9 is metadata, never a probability. If a
# wrong implementation promoted confidence to probability, the marginal would be
# 0.9 and this case's golden (and the guard test) would fail.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/profiles/probabilistic-confidence-guard/> .

ex:Patient a logic:Kind .
